Privacy Policy for WTMP - Who To Touch My Phone
Last Updated: April 28, 2026
WTMP ("we", "our", or "us") provides the "Who To Touch My Phone" mobile application. This Privacy Policy explains how we handle your information.
1. Information Collection and Use
Our app is designed with a "Local-Only" philosophy. We prioritize your privacy by keeping your data on your own device.
A. Camera Access (CRITICAL)
The app requires access to your device's Camera to perform its core security function:
•
Purpose: To capture a photo of any individual who attempts to unlock your device or successfully unlocks it while the protection service is active.
•
Handling: Captured photos are stored locally on your device's internal storage. We do not upload these photos to our servers, and we do not have access to them.
B. Usage Data
The app uses the PACKAGE_USAGE_STATS permission to identify which applications were opened during an unauthorized session. This data is stored only on your device.
C. Device Administrator
This app uses the Device Administrator permission to monitor screen unlock attempts (failed passcode/PIN). This is used solely for the purpose of triggering the security capture.
2. Data Storage and Security
•
All security logs and photos are stored within the app's private directory or your device's local storage.
•
Users can delete all logs and photos at any time using the "Purge All Logs" button in the app settings.
3. Third-Party Sharing
We do not sell, trade, or otherwise transfer your personally identifiable information or captured media to third parties. There is no third-party tracking or advertising SDKs integrated into this application.
4. Permissions
To function correctly, we request the following permissions:
•
Camera: For intruder photo capture.
•
Notifications: To maintain the background monitoring service.
•
Internet: Only for optional cloud sync (if enabled by the user).
